assets_preview/
src/guildmodel/assets/_iconcache/

# Local Claude Code settings (per-machine, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Internal design/planning references — kept local, not published. Working notes
# (teardowns, cross-app integration planning) and scratch reference geometry the
# app and test suite do not depend on (tests vendor their own fixtures under
# tests/fixtures/). Leading slash anchors each to the repo root.
/DEMO_PROJECT_TEARDOWN.md
/OLGA_TEARDOWN_AND_PLAN.md
/INTEGRATION_NOTES.md
/INCIDENT-*.md
/Current Development.png
/cnc_bed.dxf
/cnc_bed.svg
/frame_illustration.dxf
/frame_illustration.svg
/hinge_th-23_front.dxf

# Maker correspondence and the frames that came with it.
/Bug Report *.txt

# **Drawings are never committed, anywhere in the tree.** The designs are the
# maker's own product line — sold, not sample data — so a .gdraw is not ours to
# publish whatever folder it is sitting in. These patterns are deliberately
# *not* root-anchored: the earlier `/*.gdraw` only ever covered the repo root,
# which is how three drawings were nearly vendored under tests/fixtures/ as
# unpacked SVGs, a path no root-anchored rule can reach.
#
# Testing against real drawings is still supported and still worth doing — it
# is what found this season's silent defects — but by pointing the suite at a
# corpus on disk rather than by copying one in. See tests/test_frame_corpus.py
# and its GUILDMODEL_FRAME_CORPUS variable. tests/test_no_drawings_committed.py
# fails if one lands in the index anyway.
*.gdraw
*.gdraw.bak
*.gmodel

# Programs a maker sent us to look at, and programs posted at the root for a
# hand-check. Customer material — it belongs in the investigation, not the
# history. The suite's own reference program lives under tests/fixtures/, which
# this root-anchored pattern leaves alone.
/*.nc

# The engineering record: milestone history, the B-Rep evaluation, and the
# planning notes they were written against. Kept local from v1.5.0 — they are
# working documents rather than published ones, and source docstrings still
# cite them by name for anyone who has the tree.
/BUILDPLAN.md
/BUILDPLAN-NEW.md
/BREP-REWRITE-REPORT.md
/FINE-RELIEF-SAWTOOTH.md

# One-shot investigations: each was written to answer a single question, all of
# them already answered and recorded. Not build tooling — scripts/ keeps
# build_release*, make_icon and dxf_to_stl, which are.
/scripts/probe_*.py
/scripts/spike_*.py
/scripts/bench_*.py
